    "ls|LS16_S13_U_101": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 101\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 22TH DECEMBER, 2017\nNATIONAL HEALTH ACCOUNTS\n*101. SHRI ANANDRAO ADSUL:\nSHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of the per capita expenditure incurred on healthcare by the Government\nduring each of the last three years and the current year;\n(b) whether the Government has recently released any data relating to National Health\nAccounts (NHA) for 2014-15 and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether some of the States have not spent the allocated funds properly or failed to\nexpedite spending of the allocations made under various healthcare schemes to the States\nand if so, the details thereof along with the reasons therefor;\n(d) whether the Governme nt has warned these States for failing to spend the funds\nallocated under the healthcare schemes and if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and\n(e) whether the Government has issued any directions and guidelines in this regard and if\nso, the details the reof along with the steps taken by the Government to monitor the\nimplementation of Centrally Sponsored Schemes and utilisation of funds by the States?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 101* FOR 22TH DECEMBER, 2017\n(a) Per capita expenditure on healthcare by Government (Centre and States)\nfor last three years and current year, at current prices, is estimated as under:\n(i) 2014-15 - Rs. 1108\n(ii) 2015-16 - Rs. 1251\n(iii) 2016-17  (RE) - Rs. 1526\n(iv) 2017-18 (BE) - Rs. 1797\n(b) The Government has recently released data relating to National Health\nAccounts (NHA) 2014-15 and the key health financing indicators for India: NHA\nEstimates 2014-15 is  given at Annexure-I.\n(c) & (d) The State -wise release of funds and expenditure under the National\nHealth Mission (NHM) is provided at Annexure-II. A few States failed to\nutilize the released funds expeditiously. Letters were issued to the concerned\nState Governments   to utilize the funds expeditiously.\n(e) Public Health being a State subject, primary responsibility of implementation\nand monitoring of schemes under NHM rests with the State Governments.\nHowever, details of steps taken by the Central Government to monitor the\nimplementation of NHM and utilization of funds by the States are provided at\nAnnexure-III.\n\nAnnexure -I\nThe key health financing indicators for India: NHA Estimates 2014-15\nSl.\nNo.\nIndicator NHA  2014-15\n1 Total Health Expenditure (THE) as % GDP$ 3.89\n2 THE per capita (Rs.)# 3826\n3 Government Health Expenditure (GHE) as % of THE 28.96\n4 GHE as % of GDP 1.13\n5 GHE as % of General Government Expenditure (GGE)@ 3.94\n6 Per capita Government Health Expenditure (Rs.) 1108\n7 Union Government Health Expenditure as % of GHE 37\n8 State Government Health Expenditure as % of GHE 63\n9 Government based Voluntary Health Insurance as % of\nGHE\n3.28\n10 OOPE as % of THE 62.58\n11 Per capita OOPE (Rs.) 2394\n12 External/ Donor Funding as % of THE 0.7\n13 AYUSH as % of THE 14.9\nNote : (i) $ GDP value for FY 2014 -15 (Rs.1,24,33,749 Crores) – Statement 2: Second\nAdvance Estimates of National Income and Expenditures on GDP, 2016 -17;Press\nInformation Bureau Government of India Ministry of Statistics & Programme\nImplementation; 28-February-2017.\n(ii)  # The population for 2014 is projected by National Health Systems Resource\nCentre using Census population estimates- 2011 published by Office of the Registrar\nGeneral & Census Commissioner, India.\n(iii)@ GGE value for FY 2014 -15 (Rs.35,55,332 cr ores) Table 114 :  Receipts and\nDisbursements of Central and State Government, Page no. 180, Handbook of\nStatistics on Indian 