    "ls|LS16_S13_U_174": "OIH \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *174 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 29.12.2017 \n \nProtection of Tigers \n \n*174. SHRI GANESH SINGH: \n   \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is implementing any special scheme for the protection of tigers in the \ncountry; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the funds being provided to Madhya Pradesh under the said \nscheme; and  \n(c) the efforts being made by the Government to increase the amount of funds for tiger protection \nscheme as per the requirements of the States for the purpose? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n(DR. HARSH VARDHAN) \n \n \n(a), (b) & (c):- A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n*** \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a), (b) & (c) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *174 ON PROTECTION OF TIGERS DUE FOR REPLY ON \n29.12.2017 \n \n \n(a) The Government of India implements the Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Project Tiger which is \nongoing in nature through the National Tiger Conservation Authority, in association with tiger \nrange States. \n \n(b) The fund released to tiger range States under the ongoing Centrally Sponsored Scheme of \nProject Tiger during last five years and current year, State-wise, inter alia including the State of \nMadhya Pradesh is at Annexure-I. \n \n(c) Besides increase in the allocation under Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Project Tiger, there are \nprovisions in the Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 as amended in 2006, which enable States to \naugment their own resources.  As per section 38X of the said Act, Tiger Conservation \nFoundation(s) are established in individual tiger reserves.  One of their objective is to augment \nand mobilize financial resources including recycling of entry and such other fees received in a \ntiger reserve, to foster stakeholders development and eco-tourism. \n \n \n*** \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *174 ON PROTECTION OF TIGERS DUE FOR REPLY ON 29.12.2017 \n \nDetails of fund released to tiger range States under the ongoing Centrally Sponsored Scheme of \nProject Tiger during last five years and current year, including Madhya Pradesh, State-wise \n \n (Rs. in Lakhs) \n \n  \nSl. \nNo. \n  \nState \n2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \n2017-18 \n(as on \n26.12.2017) \nReleased  Released  Released  Released  Released  Released  \n1 Andhra \nPradesh 404.8904 211.7804 184.141 0.00000 173.48600 180.246 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh 420.0872 757.1705 658.4260 429.53900 597.28900 641.9432 \n3 Assam 373.894 808.9665 1509.389 1425.41300 1510.92100 1973.627 \n4 Bihar 311.064 285.0898 317.096 223.55051 487.83800 373.945 \n5 Chhattisgarh 532.4632 583.056 609.827 398.94500 626.56700 1222.871 \n6 Jharkhand 107.44023 251.168 199.08 47.98470 323.76200 262.758 \n7 Karnataka 933.5311 2016.0318 1565.7726 1378.19440 3203.61440 1757.796 \n8 Kerala 514.835 489.296 517.5351 396.60100 780.23100 506.585 \n9 Madhya \nPradesh 5772.3638 4815.734 4335.1182 1421.00700 12885.59790 7209.528 \n10 Maharashtra 848.4083 3453.3483 3425.5241 3923.07890 8229.71800 2125.406 \n11 Mizoram 468.31 233.68 232.1896 187.98450 301.54800 215.316 \n12 Odisha 163.756 786.9 707.3885 544.80052 917.16700 1193.2376 \n13 Rajasthan 4090.567 512.848 627.192 1257.80800 381.30200 598.005 \n14 Tamil Nadu 445.983 763.255 864.316 1950.17128 949.86900 799.539 \n15 Telangana - - - 214.81920 239.25900 273.76 \n16 Uttarakhand 160.69 384.045 391.19 683.98538 1023.40300 740.334 \n17 Uttar Pradesh 334.055 525.876 760.9283 624.54630 1057.04500 846.874 \n18 West Bengal 404.916 348.516 596.8825 376.50781 536.14070 570.74 \n19 Goa 0.00 2.05 0.00 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 \n  Total  16287.25423  17228.81133  17502.000    15484