    "ls|LS16_S13_U_34": " \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*34 \nFOR ANSWER ON 18/12/2017 \n \nREMOVAL OF SCRAP FROM BOKARO STEEL PLANT \n \n*34. DR. RAVINDRA KUMAR RAY: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the process of removal of  scrap from Bokaro  Steel Plant has not \nbeen started even after a lapse of one year  rendering about 500 workers as  \nunemployed; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the Government has fixed  the accountability of officers of the Steel  \nAuthority of India Limited in this regard,  if so, the details thereof and if not, the  \nreasons therefor; \n \n(d) whether the Government proposes  to cancel the contract of the company  \nwhich had not started the said work and to award it to other company; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STEEL     (SHRI CHAUDHARY BIRENDER SINGH) \n \n(a)to(e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the Lok Sabha. \n \n******** \n  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (E) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *34 FOR ANSWER ON 18/12/2017 TABLED \nBY DR. RAVINDRA KUMAR RAY , MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING \n“REMOVAL OF SCRAP FROM BOKARO STEEL PLANT” \n \n(a)&(b): The removal of scrap  in Bokaro Steel Plant (BSL) is a continuous process. \nThe last contract relating to recovery of buried scrap at Blast Furnace Slag Dump \nexpired on 07.12.2016.  SAIL has already awarded the work on 15.04.2017.  The \nSite clearance was given to the party on 28.06.2017. Successful bidders have to do \nthe job as per terms & conditions of the contract. \n \n(c)&(e):  In view of reply to (a) & (b) above, the question does not arise. \n \n******** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S13_U_35": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 35\nTO BE ANSWERED ON   15TH DECEMBER, 2017\nAARDRAM SCHEME UNDER NAVA KERALA MISSION\n35. SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has received any proposal from the Government of Kerala to\nprovide financial aid to ‘Aardram Scheme’ under Nava Kerala Mission;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the Government has sanctioned the required Financial Aid to the said mission; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the present status of the said proposal?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a): As per information received from Government of Kerala, the State has not forwarded any\nproposal for providing aid to ‘Aardram Scheme’ under Nava Kerala Mission.\n(b) to (d) Does not arise in view of (a) above.\n.....................",
    "ls|LS16_S13_U_36": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No.36 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.12.2017 \n \nVacant Posts in Higher Education Sector \n \n*36. SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE: \n \n        Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether many top management and sensitive posts in the field of Higher Education like \nUniversity Grants Commission are lying vacant; \n(b) if so, the details of such posts;  \n(c) the time from which these posts have been lying vacant, Post-wise; \n(d) whether the charges have been given for such posts and if so, the details thereof including \nthe duration of such charge for each post; and  \n(e) the steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n**** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (E) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 36 FOR 18.12.201 7 ASKED BY SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE , \nHON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT, REGARDING VACANT POSTS IN HIGHER \nEDUCATION SECTOR \n \n(a) to ( e): Filling up of vacant posts in the field of Higher Education is a continuous and \nongoing process. So far as top management and sensitive posts  in Bodies like the University \nGrants Commission is concerned, there are mainly two Regulatory Bodies in the field of Higher \nEducation under the aegis of Ministry of Human Resource Development viz. the University \nGrants Commission (UGC)  and the All India Council f or Technical Education (AICTE). T he \nobjective of UGC is to promote and co -ordinate University education and to determine and \nmaintain standards of teaching, examination and research  in Universities and AICTE aims at \nensuring coordinated and integrated development of technical and management education \nand maintenance of standards.   \n \nAt present, Prof. Anil D. Sahasrabudhe,  is the Chairman of AICTE. The post of Chairman, \nUGC had fallen vac ant on 04.04.2017 . Dr. V.S. Chauhan, the senior most Member of the \nCommission has been entrusted with the charge of Chairman, UGC w.e.f. 05.04.2017 until \nfurther orders or till a regular Chairman/Vice-Chairman is appointed or till he ceases to be a \nMember in the University Grants Commission (i.e.31.12.2017), whichever is earliest.  \n \nThe Ministry had initiated the process of filling up of the post of Chairman, UGC in October, \n2016 by constituting a Search -cum-Selection Committee  and appointment to the post of \nChairman, UGC is in advance stage of consideration of the Central Government.  \n****** ",
