    "ls|LS16_S13_U_97": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 97 \nANSWERED ON FRIDAY, THE 15TH DECEMBER, 2017/ \nAGRAHAYANA 24, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nVACANT POSTS OF DIRECTORS IN PSEs AND PSBs \n \nQUESTION \n \n97. SHRI K.N. RAMACHANDRAN: \n      SHRI BHARATHI MOHAN R. K.: \n      SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA: \n   \nWill the Minister of CORPORATE AFFAIRS                                                कारपोरेट कार्य मंत्री    \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken any steps to fill up the vacant Non-Official Part-\ntime (OPTN), women and Independent Directors in various Public Sector Enterprises \n(PSEs) and Public Sector Banks (PSBs); \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the decision taken by the Government in this regard; \n(c)  whether the Government has taken steps to include subject experts and eminent \nprofessionals in the respective fields instead of appointing on political lineage; and   \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the list of appointments made in the last three years, \nyear/company-wise? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LAW AND JUSTICE              (SHRI P. P. CHAUDHARY) \nAND CORPORATE AFFAIRS                                                                      (��������������������������������)�� \nविवि��और��न्याय��एिं��कारपोरेट��कायय��मंत्रालय��में��राज्य��मंत्री \n���������������������������������������������������� \n(a):- Appointment of Directors/Women Directors in CPSUs and PSBs are made on the \nbasis of prescribed guidelines.  Government has prescribed the time -lines for various \nassociated activities such as furnishing the proposal, processing of proposals for \nobtaining recommendations of Search Committee and processing the \nrecommendations of Search Committee for obtaining the approval of competent \nauthority to ensure timely appointments to the Boards of the CPSUs and PSBs.      \n(b) to (c): - The Government has laid down the criteria in terms of educational \nqualifications, age and experience for persons to be considered for appointment as \nnon-official Directors on the Boards of CPSEs. In te rms of laid down criteria, \nprofessionals of repute having more than 15 years of relevant domain experience in \nfields relevant to the company's area of operation and persons of eminence with proven \ntrack record from Industry, Business, Agriculture or Manage ment are eligible to be \n\nconsidered for such appointments.  For Public Sector Banks also, the guidelines for \nappointment of Non -Official Directors provide for consideration of persons from \namongst the persons of eminence with special academic training or practical \nexperience in relevant fields, chartered accountants, academicians, and retired senior \ngovernment officials.  \n(d):- Details of appointments made during the 3 years are provided at Annexure. \n \n******* \n�\n�\n�\n� �\n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN THE REPLY TO LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 97  \n \nYear 2015 \n \nA. CPSEs:- Details of Non-Official Directors  \n \nName of CPSEs Number of non-Official Directors \nAppointed \n BEML Limited 3 \n Bharat Coking Coal Limited 2 \n Bharat Dynamics Limited 2 (1 Women) \n Bharat Electronics Limited 3 (1 Women) \n Bharat Heavy Electricals Limited 3 \n Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited 3 \n Central Coalfields Limited 2 \n Central Mine Planning & Design Institute Limited 2 \n Coal India Limited 5 (1 Women) \n Eastern Coalfields Limited 1 (1 Women) \n Engineering Projects (India) Limited 2 (1 Women) \n Engineers India Limited 4 (1 Women) \n Ferro Scrap Nigam Limited 1 \n GAIL (India) Limited 3 \n Hindustan Copper Limited 4 (1 Women) \n Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited 1 \n Hindustan Shipyard Limited 1 \n Indian Oil Corporation Limited 2 \n Indian Rare Earths Limited 1 (1 Women) \n ITI  Limited 1 \n KIOCL Limited 1 \n Mahanadi Coalfields Limited 2 \n Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited 2 \n Mazagon Dock Limited 2 (1 Women) \n MECON Limited 1 \n M